{"id":"NCT07136610","title":"Standardized Application of Feeding Evaluations Using SMART Tool","official":"Standardized Application of Feeding Evaluations Using SMART Tool","summary":"Premature and medically complex infants have delayed development of oral feeding skills, leading to prolonged hospitalization, costs, and family stress. There is no \"gold standard\" infant feeding skill assessment tool for bedside clinicians. The research team developed a novel feeding skill assessment, the SMART Tool, to monitor infant feeding skill development in the neonatal intensive care unit. This study aims to determine whether this tool improves clinical outcomes, including reduced hospital days and enhanced safety and quality of infant feedings.","conditions":["Infant and Young Child Feeding"],"interventions":[{"type":"BEHAVIORAL","name":"SMART Tool"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Infants born between August 1, 2025, and July 31, 2026, AND admitted to NICU\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* No oral feeding started by July 15, 2026","minAge":"","maxAge":"1 Year","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"SUPPORTIVE_CARE","enrollment":3500,"start":"2025-08-01","pcd":"2027-07","upd":"2026-07-29","sponsor":"Wake Forest University Health Sciences","areas":["other"],"central":["Ravi Mishra, MBBS,MD,FAAP · 804.464.7472 · ravi.mishra@aah.org","Cynthia Liracrame, RN · 773.296.7977 · cynthia.liracrame@aah.org"],"sites":[{"f":"Advocate Good Shepherd Hospital","city":"Barrington","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60010","s":"R","lat":42.1539,"lon":-88.1362,"c":"Hope Reis, NPD · 804-464-7472 · hope.reis@aah.org"},{"f":"Advocate Trinity Hospital","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60617","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":"Karen Beagles, RN · 804-464-7472 · karen.beagles@aah.org"},{"f":"Advocate Sherman Hospital","city":"Elgin","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60123","s":"R","lat":42.0373,"lon":-88.2812,"c":"Cynthia Manly, RN · 804-464-7472 · cynthia.manly@aah.org"},{"f":"Advoc